                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "235510349",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198334380389",
                            "num_reviews": 10,
                            "playtime_forever": 231,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 231,
                            "last_played": 1789693855
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The worst of the MacVenture games, and I loved \"Deja Vu\" (on the NES). Moon logic puzzles, too vague of a goal, obnoxious window management that you need to re-configure every time you load a save (and you will be loading and reloading saves!), and a complete nuisance of a time limit system - especially for a game that will outright require you to just sit around burning time, waiting for something to happen. The trains are a thoroughly undue hassle, possibly outright bugged, and never seem to appear at the platforms that the schedule claims they're at. Not a worthy follow-up to the original \"Deja Vu.\"",
